// Rock shapes the ripple: it leaks through the one gap in the wall.
name Against the Wall
rule B1/S012345678
steps 4
hint Rock never changes, blocks your way, and nothing grows through it. Read the shape of what got past.
tip The wall and the left edge clip the ripple, but its top and bottom are still symmetric: the origin is level with the gap.
intro Someone raised walls here, long ago, to keep the ripples in. The walls outlasted them.
outro Stone does not grow. That is why it is still here.
map
